IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc24-appeal-right.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, Part XXI (Appeals -- Indictable Offences),
-- sections 673 to 677: Interpretation, Right of Appeal. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), part agent ccc24.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. Every function answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN (a few answer a BOOLEAN where a plain fact is built).
--   JUST TRUE   the text's words are met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, a period it fixes, a "where" gate, a flat negative).
--   NOTHING     not covered: a grant or power whose "if" gate or named complement is not met (the ruling of 2026-11-12: a function
--               named for a grant answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE), a list not closed, "includes", silent, or pointing outside the text.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into JUST FALSE.
-- FORK-TAG G1 = a function named for a grant or a power ("may") whose failed "if" gate answers NOTHING (fork line in NOTES.md);
-- FORK-TAG G2 = a "may" function whose gate is "where", "when" or "upon": answered JUST FALSE as the guide's ruling (b) has it, listed for a lawyer;
-- FORK-TAG G3 = an "entitled" function: answered as the guide's rulings give it, listed for a lawyer.
-- "The appellant" and "the person" are the individual in the seat (the accused, or the person convicted or found unfit or not criminally responsible).

§ `Part XXI -- Appeals -- Indictable Offences (sections 673 to 696)`

§§ `Section 673 -- Interpretation, definitions ("In this Part")`

-- "court of appeal" is a "means" definition that points at section 2 and adds the province of the trial.
-- The section 2 answer is the keel's `s 2 court of appeal`, called here (ccc-definitions.l4 is in this folder).
-- @tag fork=F673a
-- src:14074 | court of appeal means the court of appeal, as defined by the definition court of appeal in section 2, for the province or territory in which the trial of a person by indictment is held; (cour d’appel)
@ref s 673 "court of appeal" (src:14074-14074)
GIVEN `it is the Court of Appeal of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is the one for the province or territory in which the trial of the person by indictment is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673 court of appeal` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is the one for the province or territory in which the trial of the person by indictment is held`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "court of appeal means the court of appeal"
    ELSE `s 2 court of appeal` `it is the Court of Appeal of the province`

-- "indictment includes an information or charge in respect of which a person has been tried for an indictable offence under Part XIX": an "includes" definition,
-- so a document outside the extension is NOT COVERED here, except as section 2 "indictment" (called here) already answers.
-- @tag fork=F673i
-- src:14075 | indictment includes an information or charge in respect of which a person has been tried for an indictable offence under Part XIX; (acte d’accusation)
@ref s 673 "indictment" (src:14075-14075)
GIVEN `the document is an information or charge in respect of which a person has been tried for an indictable offence under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the document is, by section 2 indictment` IS A `s 2 indictment kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673 indictment` MEANS
    IF `the document is an information or charge in respect of which a person has been tried for an indictable offence under Part XIX`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 2 indictment` `what the document is, by section 2 indictment`   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "indictment includes"; the section 2 answer is carried through

-- src:14076 | registrar means the registrar or clerk of the court of appeal; (registraire)
@ref s 673 "registrar" (src:14076-14076)
GIVEN `the person is the registrar or clerk of the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673 registrar` MEANS
    IF `the person is the registrar or clerk of the court of appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "registrar means the registrar or clerk of the court of appeal"

-- "sentence includes (a) a declaration under 199(3), (b) an order under ..., (c) a disposition under ..., (d) an order under subsection 16(1) of the
-- Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, and (e) an order under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act."
-- Provisions of this Code are named by the core record `Provision of the Code` (rule R1); the two other Acts are plain facts.
GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`, n IS A NUMBER, sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` MEANS p's `section` EQUALS n AND p's `subsection` EQUALS sub

GIVEN p IS A `Provision of the Code`, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 673 sentence the provision is section` MEANS p's `section` EQUALS n

-- src:14077 | sentence includes
-- src:14078 | (a) a declaration made under subsection 199(3),
-- src:14079 | (b) an order made under subsection 109(1) or 110(1), section 161, subsection 164.2(1) or 194(1), section 320.24 or 462.37, subsection 491.1(2), 730(1) or 737(2.1) or (3) or section 738, 739, 742.1, 742.3, 743.6, 745.4, 745.5 or 745.52,
-- src:14080 | (c) a disposition made under section 731 or 732 or subsection 732.2(3) or (5), 742.4(3) or 742.6(9),
-- src:14081 | (d) an order made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act, and
-- src:14082 | (e) an order made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act; (sentence, peine ou condamnation)
@ref s 673 "sentence" (src:14077-14082)
GIVEN `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the order is made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673 sentence` MEANS
    IF    `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 199 "(3)"                                  -- (a)
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 109 "(1)"                                  -- (b)
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 110 "(1)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 161
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 164.2 "(1)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 194 "(1)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 320.24
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 462.37
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 491.1 "(2)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 730 "(1)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 737 "(2.1)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 737 "(3)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 738
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 739
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 742.1
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 742.3
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 743.6
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 745.4
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 745.5
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 745.52
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 731                                               -- (c)
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is section` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 732
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 732.2 "(3)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 732.2 "(5)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 742.4 "(3)"
       OR `s 673 sentence the provision is subsection` `the order or disposition is made under this provision of the Code` 742.6 "(9)"
       OR `the order is made under subsection 16(1) of the Controlled Drugs and Substances Act`                                                                        -- (d)
       OR `the order is made under subsection 94(1) of the Cannabis Act`                                                                                               -- (e)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sentence includes"

-- "trial court means the court by which an accused was tried and includes a judge or a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX."
-- "means ... and includes" is read as closed: the means limb plus the listed extension (the keel's reading, ccc-definitions.l4; see NOTES.md fork F673).
-- @tag fork=F673
-- src:14083 | trial court means the court by which an accused was tried and includes a judge or a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX. (tribunal de première instance)
@ref s 673 "trial court" (src:14083-14083)
GIVEN `the court is the court by which the accused was tried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a judge or a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 673 trial court` MEANS
    IF `the court is the court by which the accused was tried` OR `the person is a judge or a provincial court judge acting under Part XIX`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "trial court means the court by which an accused was tried"

§§ `Section 674 -- Procedure abolished`

-- A flat negative with an "other than" carve-out. JUST TRUE here means the bar applies to this proceeding.
-- Fork F674 (case by case, "(other than X)"): the authorized proceedings are taken as outside the bar in the text's own words, so the bar answers JUST FALSE for them.
-- @tag fork=F674
-- src:14087 | 674 No proceedings other than those authorized by this Part and Part XXVI shall be taken by way of appeal in proceedings in respect of indictable offences.
@ref s 674 (src:14087-14087)
GIVEN `the proceedings are by way of appeal in proceedings in respect of an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are authorized by Part XXI or Part XXVI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 674 the proceedings are barred as an appeal not authorized by Part XXI or Part XXVI` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are by way of appeal in proceedings in respect of an indictable offence`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings in respect of indictable offences"
        IF `the proceedings are authorized by Part XXI or Part XXVI`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings other than those authorized by this Part and Part XXVI"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 675 -- Right of appeal of person convicted`

-- The three grounds of appeal against conviction in 675(1)(a), and what each carries (leave, a certificate of the trial judge, or nothing).
DECLARE `s 675(1)(a) ground of appeal against conviction` IS ONE OF
    `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone`
    `s 675(1)(a)(ii) a ground that involves a question of fact or a question of mixed law and fact`
    `s 675(1)(a)(iii) a ground not mentioned in subparagraph (i) or (ii) that appears to the court of appeal to be a sufficient ground`

-- The condition each subparagraph attaches to its ground. Answers a plain BOOLEAN: it is a fact test built from facts the person can state.
-- src:14090 | (a) against his conviction
-- src:14091 | (i) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone,
-- src:14092 | (ii) on any ground of appeal that involves a question of fact or a question of mixed law and fact, with leave of the court of appeal or a judge thereof or on the certificate of the trial judge that the case is a proper case for appeal, or
-- src:14093 | (iii) on any ground of appeal not mentioned in subparagraph (i) or (ii) that appears to the court of appeal to be a sufficient ground of appeal, with leave of the court of appeal; or
@ref s 675(1)(a)(i) to (iii) (src:14090-14093)
GIVEN ground IS A `s 675(1)(a) ground of appeal against conviction`
      `leave of the court of appeal has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave of a judge of the court of appeal has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial judge has certified that the case is a proper case for appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court of appeal considers the ground a sufficient ground of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 675(1)(a) the conditions that the ground carries are met` MEANS
    CONSIDER ground
    WHEN `s 675(1)(a)(i) a ground that involves a question of law alone` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 675(1)(a)(ii) a ground that involves a question of fact or a question of mixed law and fact` THEN
        `leave of the court of appeal has been granted` OR `leave of a judge of the court of appeal has been granted` OR `the trial judge has certified that the case is a proper case for appeal`
    WHEN `s 675(1)(a)(iii) a ground not mentioned in subparagraph (i) or (ii) that appears to the court of appeal to be a sufficient ground` THEN
        `the court of appeal considers the ground a sufficient ground of appeal` AND `leave of the court of appeal has been granted`

-- 675(1)(a): "A person who is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment may appeal to the court of appeal against his conviction ..."
-- A grant. FORK-TAG G1: a failed gate (not convicted, or the ground's condition unmet) answers NOTHING.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14089 | 675 (1) A person who is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment may appeal to the court of appeal
-- src:14090 | (a) against his conviction
@ref s 675(1)(a) (src:14089-14090)
GIVEN `the person is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 675(1)(a) ground of appeal against conviction`
      `the conditions that the ground carries are met, by s 675(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(1)(a) the convicted person may appeal to the court of appeal against the conviction on the ground` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment` AND `the conditions that the ground carries are met, by s 675(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may appeal to the court of appeal"

-- 675(1)(b): against the sentence passed by the trial court, "with leave of the court of appeal or a judge thereof unless that sentence is one fixed by law".
-- Fork F675(1)(b): the "unless" is read as lifting the leave condition for a sentence fixed by law (the appeal then lies without leave); the other reading is that no appeal lies against a sentence fixed by law.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- @tag fork=F675b
-- src:14094 | (b) against the sentence passed by the trial court, with leave of the court of appeal or a judge thereof unless that sentence is one fixed by law.
@ref s 675(1)(b) (src:14094-14094)
GIVEN `the person is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence is one fixed by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(1)(b) the convicted person may appeal to the court of appeal against the sentence passed by the trial court` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted by a trial court in proceedings by indictment` AND (`leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court has been granted` OR `the sentence is one fixed by law`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with leave of the court of appeal or a judge thereof unless that sentence is one fixed by law"

-- 675(1.1): summary conviction appeals, with leave, if (a) no appeal yet against the summary conviction, (b) tried with an indictable offence, (c) an appeal lies in respect of the indictable offence.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14096 | (1.1) A person may appeal, pursuant to subsection (1), with leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court, to that court in respect of a summary conviction or a sentence passed with respect to a summary conviction as if the summary conviction had been a conviction in proceedings by indictment if
-- src:14097 | (a) there has not been an appeal with respect to the summary conviction;
-- src:14098 | (b) the summary conviction offence was tried with an indictable offence; and
-- src:14099 | (c) there is an appeal in respect of the indictable offence.
@ref s 675(1.1) (src:14096-14099)
GIVEN `leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court has been granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there has not been an appeal with respect to the summary conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summary conviction offence was tried with an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an appeal in respect of the indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(1.1) the person may appeal a summary conviction or its sentence to the court of appeal as if it had been a conviction in proceedings by indictment` MEANS
    IF    `leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court has been granted`
      AND `there has not been an appeal with respect to the summary conviction`
      AND `the summary conviction offence was tried with an indictable offence`
      AND `there is an appeal in respect of the indictable offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with leave of the court of appeal or a judge of that court"

-- 675(2): second degree murder, or manslaughter in the circumstances of any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d); life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years in excess of 10.
-- The circumstances of 236(2)(a) to (d) are a fact stated by the person (section 236 is another part's).
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14101 | (2) A person who has been convicted of second degree murder, or of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), and sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years in excess of 10 may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years in excess of 10 of their imprisonment without eligibility for parole.
@ref s 675(2) (src:14101-14101)
GIVEN `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(2) the person may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years in excess of 10 of the imprisonment without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    IF    (    `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `second degree murder`
            OR (`the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `manslaughter` AND `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)`))
      AND `the person was sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years`
      AND `the specified number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` GREATER THAN 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in excess of 10"

-- 675(2.1): "A person against whom an order under section 743.6 has been made may appeal ..." The seam to section 743.6 (ccc27) is an input (PLAN.md section 6).
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14103 | (2.1) A person against whom an order under section 743.6 has been made may appeal to the court of appeal against the order.
@ref s 675(2.1) (src:14103-14103)
GIVEN `s 743.6 the court ordered a delay in eligibility for parole` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(2.1) the person against whom an order under section 743.6 has been made may appeal to the court of appeal against the order` MEANS
    IF `s 743.6 the court ordered a delay in eligibility for parole` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person against whom an order under section 743.6 has been made"

-- 675(2.2): a person under 18 at the time of the offence, convicted of first degree murder, second degree murder or manslaughter in the circumstances of 236(2)(a) to (d), sentenced to life without parole until the period the trial judge specified.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14105 | (2.2) A person who was under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence for which the person was convicted of first degree murder, second degree murder or manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d) and was sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served the period specified by the judge presiding at the trial may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years in excess of the minimum number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole that are required to be served in respect of that person’s case.
@ref s 675(2.2) (src:14105-14105)
GIVEN `the person was under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served the period specified by the judge presiding at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified period is in excess of the minimum number of years required to be served in respect of the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(2.2) the person may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years in excess of the minimum number of years without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    IF    `the person was under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence`
      AND (    `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `first degree murder`
            OR `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `second degree murder`
            OR (`the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `manslaughter` AND `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)`))
      AND `the person was sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served the period specified by the judge presiding at the trial`
      AND `the specified period is in excess of the minimum number of years required to be served in respect of the person's case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against the number of years in excess of the minimum number of years"

-- 675(2.3): an order under subsection 745.51(1) (ccc28): the seam is an input.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14107 | (2.3) A person against whom an order under subsection 745.51(1) has been made may appeal to the court of appeal against the order.
@ref s 675(2.3) (src:14107-14107)
GIVEN `s 745.51(1) the court made an order against the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(2.3) the person against whom an order under subsection 745.51(1) has been made may appeal to the court of appeal against the order` MEANS
    IF `s 745.51(1) the court made an order against the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person against whom an order under subsection 745.51(1) has been made"

-- 675(3): a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or of unfit to stand trial: appeal on any ground in 675(1)(a)(i), (ii) or (iii), "subject to the conditions described therein".
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14109 | (3) Where a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial is rendered in respect of a person, that person may appeal to the court of appeal against that verdict on any ground of appeal mentioned in subparagraph (1)(a)(i), (ii) or (iii) and subject to the conditions described therein.
@ref s 675(3) (src:14109-14109)
GIVEN `the verdict rendered in respect of the person` IS A `Decision on the charge`
      `the conditions that the ground carries are met, by s 675(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(3) the person may appeal to the court of appeal against the verdict` MEANS
    IF    (    `the verdict rendered in respect of the person` EQUALS `a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
            OR `the verdict rendered in respect of the person` EQUALS `a verdict of unfit to stand trial`)
      AND `the conditions that the ground carries are met, by s 675(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to the conditions described therein"

-- 675(4): where a judge of the court of appeal refuses leave "otherwise than under paragraph (1)(b)", the appellant may, by filing notice in writing within seven days after the refusal, have the application determined by the court of appeal.
-- FORK-TAG G2 ("Where ..." gate: JUST FALSE by ruling (b)); the period is the text's own ("within seven days after the refusal": JUST FALSE outside it, ruling (a)).
-- Not yet filed and still within the seven days: NOTHING (the grant is limited by its own wording and has not yet been used).
-- @tag grant=where
-- @tag grant=closed
-- src:14111 | (4) Where a judge of the court of appeal refuses leave to appeal under this section otherwise than under paragraph (1)(b), the appellant may, by filing notice in writing with the court of appeal within seven days after the refusal, have the application for leave to appeal determined by the court of appeal.
@ref s 675(4) (src:14111-14111)
GIVEN `a judge of the court of appeal refused leave to appeal under section 675` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the refusal was under paragraph 675(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice in writing has been filed with the court of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days from the refusal to the filing of the notice, or to today if it has not been filed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 675(4) the appellant may have the application for leave to appeal determined by the court of appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a judge of the court of appeal refused leave to appeal under section 675`) OR `the refusal was under paragraph 675(1)(b)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judge of the court of appeal refuses leave to appeal under this section otherwise than under paragraph (1)(b)"
        IF `the number of days from the refusal to the filing of the notice, or to today if it has not been filed` GREATER THAN 7
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within seven days after the refusal"
        IF `notice in writing has been filed with the court of appeal`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by filing notice in writing with the court of appeal"

-- The same liberty as a regulative rule: the appellant MAY file within seven days of the refusal. A MAY with no LEST: lapse is FULFILLED on both stable builds.
DECLARE `s 675(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 675(4) file notice in writing with the court of appeal`

@ref s 675(4) (src:14111-14111)
`s 675(4) the appellant's liberty to have the application determined by the court of appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MAY `s 675(4) file notice in writing with the court of appeal`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The two #TRACEs of this rule are in ccc24-tests-appeal-right.l4: a filing on day 7 and a lapse at day 8 (a lapsed MAY is FULFILLED; the decision function above is what answers JUST FALSE).

§§ `Section 676 -- Right of Attorney General to appeal (what may be done to the accused or offender)`

-- 676(1)(a): acquittal, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, of a trial court in proceedings by indictment, on a question of law alone.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14113 | 676 (1) The Attorney General or counsel instructed by him for the purpose may appeal to the court of appeal
