GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 676(1)(a) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the acquittal or verdict` MEANS
    IF    `the appellant is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose`
      AND `the decision is a judgment or verdict of acquittal, or a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, of a trial court in proceedings by indictment`
      AND `the ground of appeal involves a question of law alone`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on any ground of appeal that involves a question of law alone"

