-- 676(4): second degree murder or manslaughter in the circumstances of 236(2)(a) to (d): against the number of years without eligibility for parole, being less than 25.
-- @tag grant=flip
-- src:14128 | (4) The Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose may appeal to the court of appeal in respect of a conviction for second degree murder or manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), against the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole, being less than 25, that has been imposed as a result of that conviction.
@ref s 676(4) (src:14128-14128)
GIVEN `the appellant is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 676(4) the Attorney General may appeal to the court of appeal against the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole, being less than 25` MEANS
    IF    `the appellant is the Attorney General or counsel instructed by the Attorney General for the purpose`
      AND (    `the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `second degree murder`
            OR (`the kind of homicide offence of which the person was convicted` EQUALS `manslaughter` AND `the manslaughter was in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)`))
      AND `the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole imposed` LESS THAN 25
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "being less than 25"

