§§ `Section 677 -- Specifying grounds of dissent`

-- A duty on the court. JUST TRUE: the judgment specifies the grounds in law of the dissent; JUST FALSE: it does not, though a judge dissents ("shall specify"); NOTHING where no judge dissents.
-- src:14136 | 677 Where a judge of the court of appeal expresses an opinion dissenting from the judgment of the court, the judgment of the court shall specify any grounds in law on which the dissent, in whole or in part, is based.
@ref s 677 (src:14136-14136)
GIVEN `a judge of the court of appeal expresses an opinion dissenting from the judgment of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment of the court specifies the grounds in law on which the dissent, in whole or in part, is based` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 677 the judgment of the court has specified the grounds in law of the dissent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a judge of the court of appeal expresses an opinion dissenting from the judgment of the court`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a judge of the court of appeal expresses an opinion dissenting from the judgment of the court"
        IF `the judgment of the court specifies the grounds in law on which the dissent, in whole or in part, is based`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judgment of the court shall specify any grounds in law"
